# Prune the full Wikidata dump in PHASES, saving after each one.
#
#   nohup ./build-release/bin/zelph < dev_scripts/prune-full-dump-phased.zph > run.log 2>&1 &
#   sudo /home/stefan/bin/restrict-process.sh zelph
#
# Why phases rather than one pass. The resident set does NOT fall as nodes are
# removed: the dense containers keep their capacity and the string pool is
# append-only, so a single pass holds the machine at its memory limit from the
# first minute to the last. Saving and RELOADING is what actually compacts --
# which is also why each phase ends with .new before its .load, and not merely
# with .save.
#
# The saves are the point, not a safety net. Each one is a usable artifact in
# its own right, progressively smaller and progressively more aggressive, so a
# run may be stopped after any phase and what exists is publishable. It also
# localises damage: if the acceptance check at the end comes out wrong, the
# per-phase files say which phase did it.
#
# Ordered least interesting first, so the cheap and uncontroversial removals
# happen before anything anyone might miss.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO SECTIONS OF wikidata-prune.zph ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE.
#
#   scholarly articles (Q13442814 and its section, incl. .prune-facts P1433/P921)
#   humans            (Q5 and its section, incl. .prune-facts P131)
#
# Measured on this dump they are 45.4 M and 13.1 M nodes -- 58.5 M of the
# script's ~98 M, and the great majority of its running time: at the 139
# nodes/s the scholarly-article line managed on the live dump, that line alone
# is some 90 hours. They are also the two whose removal is a judgement call
# rather than housekeeping, and humans are arguably the single most useful
# class the file has. Leaving them in is the decision this run rests on.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT MUST STILL WORK AFTERWARDS, and it is checked at the end:
# the P279 transitive-closure query of Dogan & Patel-Schneider
# (dev_scripts/test_sparql.zph). Pruning INSTANCES never removes the classes
# they are instances of, so the hierarchy should survive untouched -- but
# "should" is not "does", and the check is three lines.
#
# The reference figures, from wikidata-20260309-all-pruned.bin (9 June):
# 78 topmost culprits of 18 933 affected classes, over 1 193 228 P279 edges.
# The new artifact is a DIFFERENT one, so its numbers will differ; what must
# hold is that the query still answers, and that the class count is of the
# same order rather than collapsed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.lang wikidata
.load /home/stefan/zelph/wikidata-20260309-all.bin
.stat

# === PHASE A: the encyclopedia's own plumbing (46 lines) ===
# Categories, templates, modules, list and disambiguation pages; one item
